# wawona.io Gallery catalog

Content images on wawona.io have **one** host: Gallery (`content/gallery/<id>.md`). Landing, docs, FAQ, and posts must not hotlink `static/images/wawona-screenshots/` or pass `src=` into `screenshot`.

## Add an image

1. Put a `.jpg` in `static/images/wawona-screenshots/`.
2. Add `content/gallery/<id>.md` with **title**, **description** (required), and `extra.local_image`. Optional: `alt`, `width`, `height`.
3. Run `python3 scripts/check-gallery-refs.py` (writes `data/gallery.toml`).
4. Render with the gallery id only.

```text
Bad:  {{ screenshot(src="/images/wawona-screenshots/foo.jpg", caption="…") }}
Bad:  {{ img::optimized_image(path="images/wawona-screenshots/foo.jpg", alt="…") }}
Good: {{ screenshot(id="machines-macos") }}
```

Homepage carousel: `load_data(path="data/gallery.toml")`, then `catalog.entries | get(key="nested-plasma")` (same for other ids). Titles, alts, and paths come from that entry.

## Hard rejects

- `screenshot(src=…)` or markdown `![](/images/wawona-screenshots/…)` in docs, FAQ, posts, or templates
- Gallery page missing `description` or `extra.local_image`
- Editing `data/gallery.toml` by hand (regenerate it)
- Stretching shots: `object-fit: contain`, native width/height, no `max-height` plus `width: 100%` warp
- New screenshots as PNG (convert to `.jpg` before adding the Gallery page)

## Exception

Site chrome only: nav mark and favicon under `static/images/logo/`. Not Gallery.

See `content/gallery/_index.md` and `templates/shortcodes/screenshot.html`.
